From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:01:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Restack the popups of other threads asynchronously
 when their owner moves.

Changing the place of a window in the z-order, or showing or hiding it,
moves the pop-ups it owns along so that they stay above it; for a pop-up
of another thread that was a SetWindowPos sent to that thread, waiting
for it.  A thread that takes no messages then held up its owner: hiding
a window to destroy it waited until the other process looked at its
message queue again.

The pop-ups of other threads are now moved with SWP_ASYNCWINDOWPOS, the
way Windows has a thread on another input queue do it, and destroying
the owner returns at once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/window.c b/dlls/win32u/window.c
index 2dd991acec5..7b2c38cb714 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -4182,8 +4182,11 @@ static HWND swp_owner_popups( HWND hwnd, HWND after )
         if (list[i] == hwnd) break;
         if (get_window_relative( list[i], GW_OWNER ) != hwnd) continue;
         TRACE( "moving %p owned by %p after %p\n", list[i], hwnd, after );
+        /* a popup of another thread, maybe of another process, follows when that thread gets to it:
+         * one that takes no messages must not hold up its owner */
         NtUserSetWindowPos( list[i], after, 0, 0, 0, 0,
-                            SWP_NOMOVE | SWP_NOSIZE | SWP_NOACTIVATE | SWP_NOSENDCHANGING | SWP_DEFERERASE );
+                            SWP_NOMOVE | SWP_NOSIZE | SWP_NOACTIVATE | SWP_NOSENDCHANGING | SWP_DEFERERASE |
+                            (is_current_thread_window( list[i] ) ? 0 : SWP_ASYNCWINDOWPOS) );
         after = list[i];
     }
 
